From 83e416ed9ad2c869d78d262a42e97563e6409091 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Yu <josephyu@yahooinc.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 17:46:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Apply the log quota at startup, not only when the current
 file fills

LogRotate::init trimmed the log only inside

    if (currentSize > c_maxFileSize - c_maxLen)

so the quota was enforced when the *current* file was nearly full, and not
otherwise. After lowering c_maxSize from 100kB to 16kB the device reported

    LogRotate: found 16 log files using 60564 bytes (369%).
    Logging to /messages/log_000016.log

- the new limit was plainly in effect, since 60564/16384 is 369%, but nothing
was removed. The current file had just been created, so currentSize was small
and the condition was false. The log would have come down eventually, once
traffic filled that file and write() rotated, but every boot until then still
restored all 788 messages and paid the full 41 seconds.

Trimming unconditionally at init makes a lowered quota take effect on the next
boot instead of the next rotation. The loop and its exit condition are the ones
already used below and in write(); only the guard around them is gone.

Upstream code. Worth reporting along with the other two.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011VjqMrWWLWXvmh69rvGCEo
---
 source/util/LogRotate.cpp | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/source/util/LogRotate.cpp b/source/util/LogRotate.cpp
index e4203aa..55fd778 100644
--- a/source/util/LogRotate.cpp
+++ b/source/util/LogRotate.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,17 @@ void LogRotate::init(void)
         currentLogRead = minLogNum;
         currentLogWrite = maxLogNum;
         ILOG_INFO("LogRotate: found %d log files using %d bytes (%d%%).", numFiles, totalSize, (totalSize * 100) / c_maxSize);
+
+        // Enforce the quota on every start, not only when the current file
+        // happens to be nearly full. A log that grew under a larger quota - or
+        // one whose quota was lowered since the last boot - otherwise sits over
+        // it until enough traffic arrives to force a rotation, and every boot in
+        // between pays the full restore cost. Observed at 369% of quota after
+        // the limit was reduced, with no trimming until traffic filled the
+        // freshly-created current file.
+        while ((numFiles > c_maxFiles || totalSize >= c_maxSize) && removeLog())
+            ;
+
         if (currentSize > c_maxFileSize - c_maxLen) {
             ILOG_DEBUG("currentSize(%d) > c_maxFileSize(%d) - c_maxLen(%d)", currentSize, c_maxFileSize, c_maxLen);
             ILOG_DEBUG("numFiles(%d) > c_maxFiles(%d) || totalSize(%d) >= c_maxSize(%d)", numFiles, c_maxFiles, totalSize,
